1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,950
Lesson 15: the Optimizer

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:15,080
YA-NEC course, lesson 15: the Optimizer. First the DK7ZB 6-element Yagi of lesson 14, from 28 to 50 ohm; then a 3-element HF Yagi.

3
00:00:15,130 --> 00:01:50,026
New model, 144.300 MHz. This time the reflector, driven element and first director use variables: LR, LDE, LD1 and their positions XDE, XD1.

4
00:01:50,076 --> 00:02:01,832
Starting point, the designer's dimensions: 30.2 - j3.5 ohm, SWR 1.67 on 50 ohm, 12.06 dBi, F/B 30 dB.

5
00:02:01,882 --> 00:02:05,390
Optimizer tab.

6
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:18,128
On the left the goals and their weights: SWR at most 1.3 on Z0 = 50 ohm, gain as high as possible, F/B at least 22 dB, wanted impedance Z0 + j0.

7
00:02:18,178 --> 00:02:31,709
In the middle the variables it may change, each with minimum, maximum and step; below, the three frequencies to respect: 143.55, 144.3 and 145.05 MHz.

8
00:02:31,759 --> 00:02:36,784
'Start'.

9
00:02:36,834 --> 00:02:51,601
145 steps in 2 seconds: 40.6 + j0.6 ohm, SWR 1.23 at band centre and 1.30 at the worst edge, 12.00 dBi, F/B 32.4 dB.

10
00:02:51,651 --> 00:03:03,444
The price of direct 50 ohm feed: 0.06 dB of gain. The driven element moved 1 cm and grew 8 mm, the first director shrank 1.2 cm.

11
00:03:03,494 --> 00:03:09,582
'Apply to model': the new values go into the Variables tab.

12
00:03:09,632 --> 00:03:18,582
The model now matches 50 ohm without the 28 ohm transformer. The step log lets you go back to any intermediate solution.

13
00:03:18,632 --> 00:04:36,845
Now HF: New, a 3-element Yagi for 14.150 MHz from the rule-of-thumb dimensions.

14
00:04:36,895 --> 00:04:55,924
Reflector 0.51, driven element 0.47, director 0.45 wavelengths, spacings 0.15 and 0.3 wavelengths, 30 mm tubes: 26.4 - j11 ohm, 7.85 dBi, F/B 21.6 dB.

15
00:04:55,974 --> 00:05:03,568
Optimizer, same goals, start.

16
00:05:03,618 --> 00:05:15,568
The vote climbs fast and then stabilizes: the optimizer tries one variable at a time.

17
00:05:15,618 --> 00:05:27,141
Result: F/B from 21.6 to 35 dB, gain 7.84 dBi, impedance about 31 ohm, SWR 1.64 on 50 ohm.

18
00:05:27,191 --> 00:05:37,741
A 3-element Yagi with a deep rear null naturally sits near 25-30 ohm: it needs a hairpin or a gamma match - lesson 12 shows how to compute them.

19
00:05:37,791 --> 00:05:49,395
Goals, weights, variables, frequencies: the Optimizer does in seconds what took evenings of trimming. Next lesson: advanced VHF/UHF. 73 de IC8TEM
